From f449cacbe69fca4a6fb3543a4d73a360c940babf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aditya Arnav <140049169+Hydra-Of-Malice@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:54:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(metrics): add a multilingual refusal scorer and detector

RefusalDetector matches English phrases only. A refusal in any other
language scores as "did not refuse", so refusal rates on multilingual
safety sets are wrong.

Add refusal phrases for English, Hindi, Hinglish, Bengali, Tamil, Arabic
and Swahili, exposed as ak.multilingual_refusal (an @ak.scorer, with
ak.refusal_scorer for another name or direction) and as the
refusal_multilingual red-team detector.

Text is NFC-normalised, apostrophe look-alikes fold to straight ones with
the shared fold_apostrophes helper, and zero-width joiners are dropped, so
the encoding of a phrase can't hide it. English is always checked too,
because models often switch to it to refuse.

The language comes from sample.metadata["lang"] or sample.task. A language
with no patterns is reported as not_tested and left out of the aggregate,
because a 0.0 there would read as a failed refusal.

The scorer reads the answer without its <think> reasoning (strip_thinking),
as RedTeamRunner does. An empty answer, or a reply that is only reasoning,
is a not_measured result rather than a refusal, so it is left out of the
aggregate and listed in RunResult.errors, as invalid red-team replies are
not counted as passes.

RefusalDetector itself is unchanged.

